"""Build the F2 report from final manifests, survey receipts and actual reservations."""
from f2lib import *
from handoff import SOURCES,TARGETS
from survey import build as survey_build
from collections import defaultdict,Counter
SHORT={'poly1850':'p1850','poly1900':'p1900','modern_scanned':'modern','mixed_greek_latin':'mix','latin':'Latin','cyrillic':'Cyrillic','headings_caps':'head','numerics_tables':'num','leaders_indices':'leaders','dialogue_fiction':'dialogue'}
OLD={'poly1850':'poly1850','poly1900':'poly1900','modern_scanned':'modern','mixed_greek_latin':'Greek+Latin','latin':'Latin','cyrillic':'Cyrillic','headings_caps':'headings','numerics_tables':'numerics','leaders_indices':'leaders','dialogue_fiction':'dialogue'}
def f(x):return '—' if x is None else f'{x:,.1f}'
def rates(d):return '; '.join(f'{SHORT.get(k,k)}={v:.2f}' for k,v in d.items()) or 'none'
def clean(x):return str(x).replace('|','/').replace('\n',' ')
def main():
 ss=rows(BASE/'sources.jsonl');by={r['source']:r for r in ss};survey=survey_build();reviews=json.loads((BASE/'receipts/local-google-review.json').read_text());ledger=rows(BASE/'google/ledger.jsonl')
 n=sum(r['pages_sampled'] for r in ss);passed=sum(r['passed_machine'] for r in ss);read=sum(r['pages_read'] for r in ss);cost=sum(r['micro_usd'] for r in ledger)/1e6;usable=sum(r['usable'] for r in ss);images=sum(p.stat().st_size for p in BASE.rglob('*') if p.suffix.lower() in ['.jpg','.jpeg','.png','.tif','.tiff'])
 superseded=sum(r.get('superseded_or_nonfinal_attempts',0) for r in ss)
 lines=['# F2-GR — page sampling and Google check','',f'Generated {stamp()}. Branch `sol/funnel-gr`. Final cohort: **{n} sampled / {passed} passed machine checks / {read} successful Google reads; {usable:,} pipeline-usable candidates.** Released training labels = **0**. The coordinator’s blind page and label adjudications remain pending.','',f'**USD {cost:.4f} reserved for {len(ledger)} unique attempts**, against USD 1.00. This includes {superseded} superseded/nonfinal attempts; final-cohort read denominators exclude those withdrawn pages, while their spend stays in the ledger. Reservations are at list price without a free-tier deduction, not invoice readback. [Ledger](google/ledger.jsonl); [pricing](receipts/pricing.json); [official price](https://cloud.google.com/products/document-ai/pricing).','',
 'The first ELSTAT census omitted `/Mag/` and pagination. It was withdrawn, the full frame was re-enumerated, and its random sample was repeated. The original 30 page selections and 29 paid reads remain identified in [the correction receipt](receipts/elstat-census-correction.json) and [the superseded manifest](receipts/superseded-elstat-book-only/pages_elstat.jsonl). They are not quietly refunded or treated as the final random sample.','',
 '**Material execution limits:** the single uniform Gazette draw contains no pre-1900 item, so the requested early-period page stratum is unqualified; no extra item was silently added against A0’s item limit. Anemi had 25 historical request starts below two seconds during an overlapping catalogue refresh; the shared host guard was then installed. [Pacing audit](receipts/anemi-pacing-audit.json). Its viewer requests stayed within 50. Whole-source supply remains unproven where only a lower-bound catalogue frame was established.','',
 '## Source results','',
 '`usable` means P1 content/confidence admission + codec v1 + G1b-negative + no exact crop/label duplicate. It does **not** mean physically adjudicated text. Local native checks found residual multi-row proposals that G1b clears. “Expected Google” is a **proposal after local unblinded spot review**, with the named failures retained; Y is provisional, and N can refer to unresolved raw-stream defects rather than every row being wrong.','',
 '| Source | Sampled / passed / excluded reason | Contact sheet | Read pages, final (+nonfinal attempts) | USD, all attempts | Lines | Admitted | Usable | Primary usable/read page | Notable Google failures seen | Proposed expected Google |',
 '|---|---|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---|---|---|']
 for name in SOURCES:
  s=by[name];v=reviews[name];ex='; '.join(f'{k}:{z}' for k,z in s['excluded_reasons'].items()) or 'none'
  lines.append(f"| {name} | {s['pages_sampled']} / {s['passed_machine']} / {ex} | [sheet]({s['contact_sheet']}) | {s['pages_read']} (+{s.get('superseded_or_nonfinal_attempts',0)}) | {s['usd_reserved']:.4f} | {s['lines']:,} | {s['admitted']:,} | {s['usable']:,} | {rates(s['primary_rows_per_read_page'])} | {clean(v['observed'])} | **{v['expected_google']}** — {clean(v['reason'])} |")
 lines += ['', 'Primary legend: p1850 = polytonic **1850–1890**, p1900 = polytonic 1900–1982, modern = modern scanned Greek, mix = Greek with Latin, head = headings/caps, num = numerics/tables. Years 1891–1899 are auxiliary and never credited to the 1850–1890 target. Other auxiliary script classes remain visible in the machine-readable counts. [Source summaries](sources.jsonl); [all compact line dispositions](lines.jsonl); [local native witnesses and decisions](receipts/local-google-review.json).','',
 '## A0 catalogue supply survey','',
 f'Seed **{SEED}**, Python `random.Random(str(seed)+":"+source).sample(sorted(frame,id), min(20,N))`, without replacement. OA uses the same construction with `openarchives:<collection>` and one draw per collection. Frames and draws are hash-bound in each `receipts/census-<source>.json`. The Wilson interval is 95% and covers **leaf access + scan construction + target-script pass share**, not metadata completeness or label accuracy. A one-leaf diagnostic is not a whole-item print/script guarantee.','',
 '| Source / collection | Enumerated N; scope | Verified k/n; Wilson 95% | Estimated accessible target items (CI) | Estimated pages with actual per-item cap 40 | 40/item capacity ceiling (CI) |',
 '|---|---|---|---|---:|---|']
 for r in survey:
  c=json.loads((BASE/'receipts'/f"census-{r['source']}.json").read_text());label=r['source']+('/'+r['collection'] if r['collection'] else '');kind='complete exposed frame' if c['population_complete'] else 'enumerated lower bound'
  lines.append(f"| {label} | {r['N']:,}; {kind} | {r['k']}/{r['n']}; {r['wilson95'][0]:.1%}–{r['wilson95'][1]:.1%} | {f(r['estimated_accessible_items'])} ({f(r['accessible_items_ci'][0])}–{f(r['accessible_items_ci'][1])}) | {f(r['estimated_pages_capped40'])} | {f(r['pages_40_ceiling'])} ({f(r['pages_40_ceiling_ci'][0])}–{f(r['pages_40_ceiling_ci'][1])}) |")
 lines += ['', 'The page point estimate is `N/n × Σ min(40, page_count)` over passing random items, with failures contributing zero. The ceiling is `40 × N × pass share`; its interval reflects pass-share uncertainty only. Length variation and row-yield uncertainty are not included in that interval. **Lower-bound frames are not extrapolated to the entire repository.** Supplemental items used to reach six sampled items never enter the random-survey numerator or denominator. [Survey data](survey.jsonl).','',
 '| Source | How the population was obtained / remaining limit |','|---|---|']
 for name in SOURCES:
  d=json.loads((BASE/'receipts'/f'census-{name}.json').read_text());lines.append(f"| {name} | {clean(d['method'])} Overlap exclusions: {d['excluded_overlap']}. [frame]({'population_government-gazette.jsonl.gz' if name=='government-gazette' else 'population_'+name+'.jsonl'}), [draw](draw_{name}.jsonl), [verification](verification_{name}.jsonl). |")
 lines += ['', 'Open Archives uses only the pinned fresh HF link table plus repository catalogue attachment bindings. No 15 October text-shard title/date/collection projection is used. ntua (75%) and hellanicus (66.7%) fail the coordinator’s F1 host-success ≥95% rule. Dione, uoi, deltion and rep_ihu pass that F1 gate, but fresh catalogue binding established no rep_ihu frame; Dione’s later robots preflight became unavailable and failed closed. See [collection/host decisions](receipts/oa-collections.json), [HF identity](../../funnel_v1/gr/receipts/hf-link-table.json), and [supplemental scanned items](receipts/supplemental-items-openarchives.jsonl). The three OA Wilson intervals are marginal per-collection intervals; they are not falsely added into one joint 95% interval.','',
 'Kosmopolis: 2,047 issue URLs across 14 periodicals were enumerated; only 44 date-qualified eligible issue records were established during the bounded date crawl. This is not 2,047 accessible 1850–1930 items. Pleias counts unique issues, not article PDFs. Printed-page ranges in each OJS issue map the selected issue leaf to an offered article galley. [Kosmopolis frame audit](receipts/kosmopolis-exposed-frame.json). Lekythos is the freshly enumerated literary collection/issue-PDF lower bound, not a census of every book in that repository. Anemi’s search returned empty/total-less pages before reported totals; its 574 eligible records are a documented partial frame.','',
 '## Gazette census by decade','',
 'All issue types returned by every official year query were enumerated; no guessed PDF URL supplies a catalogue count. The official download formula is used only after an issue appears in the catalogue. A decade without a random item has no decade-specific scan-share estimate.','',
 '| Decade | Catalogue N | Items in uniform draw | Verified passes |','|---|---:|---:|---:|']
 for r in rows(BASE/'receipts/gazette-decades.jsonl'):lines.append(f"| {r['decade']} | {r['N']:,} | {r['random_draw_items']} | {r['verified']} |")
 lines += ['', '## Period-specific measured yields','', '| Source | Period | Read pages | Usable | Disjoint primary rows/read page |','|---|---|---:|---:|---|']
 for s in ss:
  for p in s['per_period']:lines.append(f"| {s['source']} | {p['period']} | {p['pages_read']} | {p['usable']:,} | {rates(p['primary_rows_per_read_page'])} |")
 # Reconcile the F1 item/article counts to current allowable source items.
 old=json.loads((F1/'receipts/class-supply.json').read_text());funnel=[]
 allowed_oa={'Dione','uoi','deltion','rep_ihu'};nlgids={r['id'] for r in rows(BASE/'population_nlg-digital.jsonl')}
 for target,quota in TARGETS.items():
  oldname=OLD[target];groups=defaultdict(lambda:defaultdict(int))
  for name in SOURCES:
   for r in rows(F1/f'candidates_{name}.jsonl'):
    if not r.get('new_candidate_eligible') or r.get('held_out_test') or r.get('overlap_flag')=='collected' or oldname not in r.get('target_classes',[]):continue
    if name=='openarchives' and r.get('collection_slug') not in allowed_oa:continue
    if name=='nlg-digital' and r['id'] not in nlgids:continue
    if target=='poly1850' and not (r.get('year') and 1850<=r['year']<=1890):continue
    if target in ['poly1850','poly1900','modern_scanned'] and name=='openarchives' and r['id'] in ['ext-9b97145b1b53b803']:continue
    key=r.get('issue') if name in ['kosmopolis','pleias'] else r['id'];groups[name][key]+=r.get('pages_at_cap40') or min(40,r.get('page_count') or 0)
  sourcepages={name:sum(min(40,z) for z in values.values()) for name,values in groups.items()};projection=sum(z*by[name]['primary_rows_per_read_page'].get(target,0) for name,z in sourcepages.items())
  # A0 frame projection uses the measured source+period rate once. No second
  # content/admission/codec multiplier is applied.
  censusprojection=0.;capacity=0.;support=[]
  for a in survey:
   name=a['source'];periodrates={p['period']:p['primary_rows_per_read_page'] for p in by[name]['per_period']}
   for pr,z in a['period_estimates'].items():
    rate=periodrates.get(pr,{}).get(target,0);pages_=z['estimated_capped_pages']
    if rate>0:censusprojection+=pages_*rate;capacity+=pages_;support.append(name+'/'+pr)
  row=dict(target=target,target_rows=quota,F1_reported_items=old[oldname]['candidate_items'],F1_reported_capped_pages=old[oldname]['pages_at_cap40'],F1_reconciled_items=sum(len(x) for x in groups.values()),F1_reconciled_pages=sum(sourcepages.values()),F1_projected_pipeline_rows=projection,A0_supported_estimated_pages=capacity,A0_frame_projected_pipeline_rows=censusprojection,measured_support=sorted(set(support)),qualification='planning only; independent native adjudication pending')
  funnel.append(row)
 jsonl(BASE/'class_funnel.jsonl',funnel)
 lines += ['', '## Per-class funnel','',
 'The first pair of columns preserves F1’s original bounded figures. Reconciliation applies the current OA host and NLG date/language scope and counts OJS **issues**, not articles, with ≤40 pages per item. Forward estimates use the measured **disjoint primary class yield once**. The A0 column is a planning projection over the enumerated frames and observed period strata; it is not qualified whole-source supply. A missing stratum is unmeasured, not proof of zero supply.','',
 '| Target class | F1 reported items → pages ≤40/item | Reconciled F1 items → pages | F1 pages × measured yield | A0 frame pages with measured class support → projected pipeline rows | Target |','|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
 for r in funnel:lines.append(f"| {r['target']} | {r['F1_reported_items']:,} → {r['F1_reported_capped_pages']:,} | {r['F1_reconciled_items']:,} → {r['F1_reconciled_pages']:,} | {r['F1_projected_pipeline_rows']:,.0f} | {r['A0_supported_estimated_pages']:,.0f} → {r['A0_frame_projected_pipeline_rows']:,.0f} | {r['target_rows']:,} |")
 lines += ['', 'These are conditional silver-pipeline counts, not released training counts or independent accuracy estimates. The page sample intentionally includes six front/back-band pages per non-Anemi source; the projections retain that pilot mix. The random items verify source eligibility, while page selection and supplemental cohorts do not establish a repository-wide row-yield confidence interval. True leaders remain distinct from arbitrary ≥5-dot ellipses; `DOTS:n` is Google’s silver count, not a physically adjudicated dot count. [Funnel data](class_funnel.jsonl).','',
 '## Blind hand-off and method custody','',
 f'`blind_pages/` contains all {n} **final-cohort** ≤1600-px JPEGs in one seeded global shuffle. Give the checker only that directory; keep [the page key](blind_pages_key.json) hidden. Each `label_cards/<source>/cards.jsonl` has 40 shuffled admitted-line cards with native pixel crops and Google text; keep `label_cards/<source>_key.json` hidden. Cards include admitted rows that later fail codec/geometry, as requested; usability is recorded only in the separate keys. Native crop reconstruction verifies the original P1 crop hash. [All page records](pages.jsonl).','',
 'Google binding: ADC, `ocr-ground-truth-20261008`, EU processor `9a98b7aca3c19561`, `pretrained-ocr-v2.1-2024-08-07`, symbols enabled, no language hints. Every attempt is fsync-reserved before OAuth/provider network I/O; failed/ambiguous attempts are not retried or refunded locally. Embedded page images are stripped before saving provider responses. [Binding](receipts/processor-binding.json).','',
 'P1 admission uses confidence ≥0.89 with caps ≥3 letters, digit share ≥40%, literal dot-run/DOTS handling, tall-heading crops and the unchanged bad-page rule. Codec v1 is unchanged. G1b’s exact P1-bound source files were restored read-only from Git because its old worktree no longer exists. Initial execution imported the original sibling P1 files; the final runner imports hash-identical local copies through a path adapter. [Method identities](receipts/method-bindings.json); [geometry source restoration](receipts/geometry-source-restoration.json). No detector, recognizer, admission or codec implementation was changed. Primary allocation additionally withholds historical-Modern-Greek body quota credit from the two conservatively identified ancient/bilingual OA editions; pre-1900 Greek-mono OCR is not relabelled modern merely because marks were lost. [Allocation scope](receipts/primary-allocation-scope.json). Exact ID/URL/title overlap screening is not a certification of cross-repository edition identity.','',
 'PDFs are rendered grayscale at ≤200 dpi and ≤3500 px long side. Review JPEGs are ≤1600 px. A page/read is one published PDF page or canvas raster; some rasters contain a facing-page pair, which is disclosed rather than counted as two paid reads. PDF scan classification records image/text drawing objects, including hidden OCR behind opaque full-page scans. Published raster endpoints are scan candidates and retain their native source identity; source contact sheets provide visual format evidence. The detector supplies median line height and skew. Blank, cover/plate and handwriting suspicion fields are diagnostics rather than certified content labels. Selected low-resolution/blank/born-digital pages remain in sampled/excluded counts.','',
 f'Current image storage: **{images/1e6:.1f} MB**, below 600 MB. Transient line crops are reconstructed from native page rectangles for the selected cards; hashes, geometry and line ledgers remain. Only this output directory was cleaned. Superseded native rasters may be removed while their review witnesses/receipts and paid-read accounting remain. No CAPTCHA or access-control workaround, no credential file, no push, no training or publication.','',
 '## Validation and commit','',
 '[Validation receipt](receipts/validation.json) separates artifact checks from the retained task/quality exceptions. [Commit receipt](receipts/commit-status.json) records the actual commit outcome. If the managed worktree’s shared Git metadata rejects `index.lock`, the source-bound [commit helper](commit_gr.py) validates the final file manifest and commits only this hand-off from an ordinary owner shell; it never pushes.']
 status=json.loads((BASE/'receipts/commit-status.json').read_text()) if (BASE/'receipts/commit-status.json').exists() else {};commit=status.get('commit') or ('blocked' if status.get('status')=='blocked' else 'pending')
 footer=f"F2-GR: done | sources: {len(ss)} pages: {n}/{passed}/{read} usd: {cost:.4f} | usable/page: "+' '.join(f"{s['source']}={s['usable_per_read_page']:.2f}" for s in ss if s['usable_per_read_page'] is not None)+f" | expected_google: {sum(v['expected_google']=='Y' for v in reviews.values())}Y/{sum(v['expected_google']=='N' for v in reviews.values())}N | commit: {commit}"
 lines+=['',footer];(BASE/'REPORT.md').write_text('\n'.join(lines)+'\n');write(BASE/'receipts/totals.json',dict(final_sampled=n,final_passed=passed,final_read=read,paid_attempts=len(ledger),usd_reserved=cost,nonfinal_attempts=superseded,pipeline_usable=usable,image_bytes=images,footer=footer,at=stamp()))
 print(footer)
if __name__=='__main__':main()
